{"strongs": "H2611", "word": "חָנֵף", "translit": "cha.neph", "root": "חנף", "morph": "H:A", "pos": "adjective", "gloss": "profane, irreligious", "definition": "חָנֵף adjective profane, irreligious (Syriac profane, hence often Healthen, apostate ; Arabic inclining to a right state , especially the true religion a Muslim ) — absolute ׳ ח Job 8:13 + 10 t.; plural חֲנֵפִים Isa 33:14 חַנְפֵי Job 36:13 ; Ps 35:16 — profane, godless: of persons, ׳ אָדָם ח Job 34:30 ׳ גּוֺי ח Isa 10:6 as substantive godless man Isa 9:16 (|| מרע ) Job 8:13 ; Job 13:16 ; Job 17:8 ; Job 20:5 ; Job 27:8 ; Prov 11:9 collective ׳ עֲדַת ח Job 15:34 plural Isa 33:14 חַנְפֵילֵֿב Job 36:13 בְּחַנְפֵי לַעֲגֵי מָעוֺג Ps 35:16 as profane men, mockers for cake (i.e. table-jesters; on construct see Ges § 130. 5 ), but text dubious (see Che critical note Bae ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2960')\">BDB2960</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2611')\">H2611</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2959')\">BDB2959</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2961')\">BDB2961</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חָנֵף</bdbheb> <b>adjective</b> <highlightword>profane, irreligious</highlightword> (Syriac <placeholder1865/> <highlight>profane, hence often Healthen, apostate</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder1866/> <highlight>inclining to a right state</highlight>, especially <highlight>the true religion a Muslim</highlight>) — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 8:13\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(18,8,13)\">Job 8:13</ref> + 10 t.; plural <bdbheb>חֲנֵפִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 33:14\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(23,33,14)\">Isa 33:14</ref> <bdbheb>חַנְפֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 36:13\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(18,36,13)\">Job 36:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 35:16\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"3